# Copy to .env and uncomment what you want to change.
# Loaded by the Makefile (-include .env) and exported into every make target,
# so `make run`, `make dev`, and `make test` all pick it up.
# Plain KEY=value lines only (no `export`, no quotes, no `~`). Built-in defaults
# are shown below; leaving everything commented changes nothing.

# Hugging Face token — only needed if the model isn't already in your HF cache.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx

# How much transcript in front of the playhead turns the caught-up indicator
# green. Display only: the worker always transcribes the whole file, so this
# does not gate or pause anything.
# LT_LOOKAHEAD=10.0
# LT_CHUNK=30.0
# LT_REMUX=1
# LT_TRANSLATE_MODEL=mlx-community/whisper-large-v3-mlx

# Read-along: speak the English translation over the video. Off by default —
# the Kokoro weights are a ~350 MB one-time download the first time you press
# Speak, and espeak-ng must be installed (brew install espeak-ng). Point these
# at your espeak-ng if it isn't in a Homebrew prefix.
# LT_TTS=1
# LT_TTS_MODEL=mlx-community/Kokoro-82M-4bit
# LT_TTS_VOICE=af_heart
# LT_TTS_LANG=a
# PHONEMIZER_ESPEAK_LIBRARY=/opt/homebrew/lib/libespeak-ng.dylib
# PHONEMIZER_ESPEAK_DATA_PATH=/opt/homebrew/share/espeak-ng-data

# Chapters: a local MLX model names the topic once per window of transcript. It
# runs in this process on the chapter worker thread — no server to start.
# Nothing happens unless the weights are ALREADY in the HF cache — the app never
# triggers a multi-GB pull — so `huggingface-cli download <model>` once, or point
# LT_CHAPTER_MODEL at a local weights dir. Weights load on the first window and
# then stay resident next to Whisper.
# AIM is how much transcript one call sees; MIN/MAX clamp it. A chapter appears
# one window after you watch that much, and every window when transcription ends.
# LT_CHAPTER_MODEL=mlx-community/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-4bit
# LT_CHAPTER_AIM=300
# LT_CHAPTER_MIN=180
# LT_CHAPTER_MAX=480

# Absolute path, not ~ — the app does not expand the tilde.
# LT_CACHE=/Users/you/.cache/overhear-subs

# Ceiling on the whole cache directory, in MB. The app prunes least-recently-used
# entries at boot and after every open until it fits; each entry is one video's
# PCM (~230 MB per hour) plus, if it needed remuxing, a full converted copy. The
# currently-open video is never pruned. 0 disables pruning entirely.
# LT_CACHE_MAX=4096

# PORT=8000
